WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.480
Although he's best remembered for his contributions
to sci-fi television as creator of Star Trek,

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.920
many of Gene Roddenberry's show concepts never
got off the ground.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.180
After his death in 1991, his widow Majel Barrett
discovered a stash of Roddenberry's scripts

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.660
and notes for some of these proposed shows—one
of which became Sci-Fi Channel's hit series,

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.660
Andromeda.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.739
With over 100 episodes wrapping up over a
decade ago in 2005, here's what the stars

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:25.289
of Andromeda are up to today!

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:26.979
Kevin Sorbo

00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:30.889
As one of the elite High Guard of the Systems
Commonwealth, Kevin Sorbo's Captain Dylan

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:35.039
Hunt and his starship Andromeda Ascendant
were responsible for protecting the planets

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:39.690
and inhabitants of three galaxies, until his
leap 300 years into the future.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.969
After the series ended, Sorbo, who was previously
best known for playing Hercules, continued

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:48.429
building upon his prolific acting career with
appearances in The O.C., Meet the Spartans,

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:50.300
and many other films and TV shows.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.249
Additionally, Sorbo lent his voice to several
video game characters in titles like Skylanders:

00:00:55.249 --> 00:00:59.890
SuperChargers, and has reprised his role as
Hercules in the God of War game franchise.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.399
Most recently, you can spot Sorbo in Supergirl.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:04.780
Lisa Ryder

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.191
Lisa Ryder's Beka Valentine had never been
interested in saving the galaxy—until she

00:01:09.191 --> 00:01:13.710
crossed paths with Captain Dylan Hunt, and
she became a loyal member and First Officer

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.900
of the Andromeda crew.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.189
These days, the Canadian-born Ryder is still
working as an actress.

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:22.600
She's appeared in over a dozen different roles
in TV and film — most recently, Nurse Greenwood

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.820
in the FX horror series The Strain.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.690
Additionally, Ryder has returned to theatre
where she got her start.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.750
Her play Wild Oxen was featured in a workshop
reading during the 2017 Groundswell Festival

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.470
in Toronto.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.020
Laura Bertram

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.770
At the start of the series, the purple-skinned
humanoid alien Trance Gemini—played by Canadian

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.820
actress Laura Bertram—had a bubbly and effusive
personality, only later transforming to reveal

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.050
her true nature.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.470
Since the end of the series, Bertram has enjoyed
a successful acting career.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:54.530
You may have spotted her in guest roles on
the popular shows Supernatural and Once Upon

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.579
a Time, or in her recurring role on the Hallmark
Channel's When Calls The Heart.

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:02.429
Additionally, Bertram is a high school teacher
in British Columbia, as well as an instructor

00:02:02.429 --> 00:02:05.770
at Biz Studio screen-acting school in Vancouver.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.479
Gordon Michael Woolvett

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:12.150
After the fall of the Commonwealth, Boston-born
Seamus Harper, played by Gordon Michael Woolvett,

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.910
escaped from the Nietzscheans, and eventually
ended up as a crewman for Valentine.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.970
Woolvett has since appeared on Supernatural,
the Canadian drama The Guard, and the CW horror-comedy

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:21.970
series, iZombie.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.250
Woolvett is also comfortable behind the camera
as a director, as evidenced by his 2017 documentary

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.350
Around the World in 80 Anthems.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.470
Lexa Doig

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:35.800
Known affectionately by the crew as "Rommie,"
the android avatar of the powerful artificial

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.330
intelligence within the ship Andromeda Ascendant
was portrayed by Toronto native Alexandra

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.330
Doig.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.590
Following her stint on Andromeda, Doig has
continued to work on several sci-fi TV shows,

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:49.820
including Supernatural, Stargate SG-1, V,
and Continuum.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.310
Fans may remember her from the 2002 horror
film Jason X.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.480
Most recently, Doig appeared on Arrow as well
as The Arrangement.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.180
Keith Hamilton Cobb

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.740
Among the Andromeda crew, ruthless Nietzschean
mercenary Keith Hamilton Cobb's Tyr Anasazi

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.810
was a fascinatingly complicated character
to pin down.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.700
Cobb left the series after the fourth season,
and immediately transitioned into his role

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.980
as Damon Porter on The Young and the Restless.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.270
Cobb then moved on to Logo's Noah's Arc, and
CSI: Miami.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.790
In recent years, Cobb has returned to the
theatre, penned a number of short stories

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.700
and other written works, and is currently
touring his one man show, American Moor.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.160
Steve Bacic

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.540
Nietzschean weapons officer Telemachus Rhade,
played by Steve Bacic, was a latecomer to

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.090
the Andromeda crew, having joined Captain
Dylan Hunt in season two.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.350
Following his spot on the series, Bacic continued
in his career with Hallmark's All for Love,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.470
Blade: The Series, The Guard, and HBO's Big
Love.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:45.690
Most recently, he reunited with Lexa Doig,
in an episode of Arrow.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.210
Brandy Ledford

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.240
The android Doyle, played by Brandy Ledford,
debuted on the show when she was built by

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.620
Seamus Harper while he was stranded with a
malfunctioning Rommie.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.270
After the series, former model Ledford appeared
on Canadian mystery drama Whistler, Stargate:

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.300
Atlantis, Modern Family, and NCIS: Los Angeles.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.610
Thanks for watching!

